<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14963" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dū^pondĭus</span></b> , ii,
			m., or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dŭpondĭum</span></b> , ii (cf.
			<i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 9, 49, § 81</span></i>; also,
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dĭpon-dĭum</span></b> , Gromat. Vet. p. 28, 14; p.
		167, 11), n.
		duo-pondus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the sum of two</i> asses. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> As a coin, <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 169</span></i>; <i><span class="en">9, §
			81</span></i> Müll.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 33, 3, 13, § 42</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Cic. Quint. 16, 53</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Petr. 14, 3
			al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>need</i>, <i>want</i>, <i><span class="en">Petr. 58,
			13</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			As a measure, <i>two feet</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 3, 13,
				5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 15,
			2</span></i> et saep.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
